### Task 5: Automatic Compiled Model Cache

**Files:** Create `Sources/Models/Internal/ModelCache.hpp`, `ModelCache.cpp`; modify `Sources/Models/Models.cpp`; extend tests.

**Produces in `Models::Internal::ModelCache`:**
```cpp
struct Payload { std::vector<std::uint8_t> bytes; };
bool load(const std::string& source, Formats::Document *document, std::string *error = nullptr);
bool encode(const std::string& source, const Formats::Document& document, Payload *payload, std::string *error = nullptr);
void writeAsync(const std::string& source, Payload payload);
std::filesystem::path pathFor(const std::string& source);
}
```

**Important ownership rule:** `encode()` runs while the imported `Formats::Document` still exists and creates an owned byte payload. The worker receives only that owned payload and performs file I/O/atomic rename; no worker may retain a reference into a document that `storeModel()` is about to move from.

- [ ] Write RED cache round-trip tests using a small `Formats::Document`; verify meshes/nodes/scenes/material values and texture source graph round-trip.
- [ ] Write RED invalidation/corruption tests that mutate source, external `.bin`, referenced external texture size/mtime, schema version and payload bytes independently.
- [ ] Implement platform roots: macOS `~/Library/Caches/Horse/Models`, Linux `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/Horse/Models` else `~/.cache/Horse/Models`, Windows `%LOCALAPPDATA%/Horse/Models`. Allow an internal/test environment override `HORSE_MODEL_CACHE_DIR` so tests never touch the real user cache.
- [ ] Use a stable 64-bit hash of normalized absolute source path for the filename. Cache header contains fixed magic, schema/importer version, payload length/checksum and bounded section counts.
- [ ] Encode normalized `Formats::Document` runtime data plus a dependency manifest. Build the texture table by recursively asking `TextureStreaming` for descriptors of texture handles referenced by every material/variant; external texture descriptors become cache dependencies. `Document::dependencies` contributes external buffers.
- [ ] Decode texture descriptors first and recreate stable deferred texture handles, then reconstruct material handles inside the decoded `Formats::Document` using cache-local texture IDs.
- [ ] Validate all counts/lengths/overflow before allocating. Any bad header/version/checksum/dependency is a clean cache miss.
- [ ] `writeAsync()` queues only owned payload + target path; worker creates parent directories, writes a unique temporary file, closes it and atomically renames it. Failure is diagnostic-only.
- [ ] Integrate `Models::load()`: memory cache -> compiled cache -> source loader. On source success, `encode()` an owned payload, queue `writeAsync()`, then move the document into existing `storeModel()`.
- [ ] Verify cache tests GREEN and commit: `Add compiled model cache`.

